          "The PMC Operator: This is a composite character speaking in the detached, professional jargon of the privatized military industry. His lyrics are cold and transactional, focused on the contract, the payment, and the mission objectives. He is the embodiment of \"the business face of war.\" Beneath the professional veneer, however, there are flashes of the moral injury he denies feeling—the guilt and shame that are not part of the contract.",
