      "decorated_lyrics_text": "[Genre: Epic Post-Rock, Industrial Folk, Cinematic, Dark Americana]\n[Mood: Somber, building to Furious, Chaotic, and finally Desolate]\n[Vocalist: Male, starts as a Weary Storyteller, becomes a Cynical Sneer, ends in a Raw, Desperate Scream]\n[Tempo: Starts slow 80bpm, builds to 160bpm]\n[Part 1: The Human Cost]\n[Instrumentation: mournful acoustic guitar, style of Track 1 'Lordstown']\n[Vocalist: Male]\n[Vocal Delivery: Sung, weary, intimate storyteller]\nRemember the man from Lordstown, with the promise in his eye?\nForced to sell his home and wave his family goodbye\nRemember the taste of water, the poison in the well?\nA dollar for the deed that led a child to hell\nRemember Newton's ghost and the life that Maytag made?\nA pension promise broken, a future betrayed\nThese aren't just stories, they're not from long ago\nThey're the roots of the sickness that we all watched grow\n[Part 2: The System's Logic]\n[Tempo increases to 120bpm]\n[Instrumentation: a cold industrial drum machine and pulsing synth bass enter, style of Track 5 'Unwarranted Influence']\n[Vocalist: Male]\n[Vocal Delivery: becomes a colder, rhythmic, cynical sneer]\n[Musical Sample: a faint, distorted synth loop from 'The SACKLER Act' plays underneath]\nThen came the warning of a misplaced power's rise\nReflected in the profits in a contractor's eyes\nThe business face of war, the market for all fear\nWhile the house that Oxy built just reappears each year\nAnd the watchdog in the hallway, he's been declawed and tamed\nIn a game of \"capture\" where the public gets blamed\nIt's a balance sheet of ruin, a soul that can't be found\nAs they strip it all for parts and sell it by the pound\n[Part 3: The Reckoning]\n[Tempo accelerates further to 160bpm]\n[Instrumentation: Distorted guitars and crashing drums enter, building a wall of sound]\n[Soundscape: faint, echoing whispers of lyrical lines from every song on the album begin to swirl in the background, creating a chaotic collage]\n[Vocalist: Male]\n[Vocal Delivery: becomes more desperate and powerful]\nAnd what's the cost of conscience in a dimensional hell?\nAnother line item that the politicians sell\nWhile the signal's drowned in noise, a frantic, cheap debate\nAs they trade upon the knowledge of a nation's failing state\nFrom the factory floor to the forgotten soldier's plea\nFrom the poison in the ground to the halls of bribery\nEvery gear in the machine is greased with human pain\nAgain, and again, and again, and again!\n[Crescendo]\n[Instrumentation: Becomes a massive, chaotic wall of sound. Orchestral strings, industrial noise, and screaming guitar feedback join the chaos.]\n[The swirling lyrical samples become a deafening roar.]\n[Vocalist: Male]\n[Vocal Delivery: a raw, throat-shredding, sustained scream]\nWHEN THE BOOKS ARE BALANCED!\nWHEN THE FINAL PRICE IS TOLD!\nWHEN EVERY SINGLE PIECE OF US IS BOUGHT AND SOLD!\nWHAT ARE WE WORTH?!\n[Outro]\n[The wall of sound abruptly cuts to total silence.]\n[Sound effect: the desolate, lonely sound of wind blowing through a broken window in a vast, empty, abandoned factory. It continues for 10 seconds.]\n[Fade to complete silence.]",
